# Berserker's bigger blood (1.1.2, the project owner, 24.11.2026: "größere Blutfontäne und größere Blutlache bei
# Treffern, rund 1.5x"; runtime/berserker.cpp): the blood of a hit on an enemy 1.5 times as big while Berserker plays.
# - em_sub.cpp EmDmBloodSet / EmDmBloodSet2 / EmDmBloodSet3 and em10.cpp em10BloodSet / em1cBloodSet: a scope
#   (Re4BloodScope) around the game's blood helpers of a hit (em10.cpp without new lines: byte_views.json and
#   lp64_int_casts.json find their sites near the recorded lines);
# - est.cpp EstSet and esp_sub.cpp EspEstSetSelect: inside that scope, for an enemy and on Berserker, the game's own
#   ESPSEQ_CONTROL with the size multiplied by 1.5 (copied into the sequence and its sub-effects, the floor blood too);
# - esp_sub.cpp EspSeqSet: Berserker's control only for the blood sprites (ids 0x00, 0x01, 0x0B, 0x10).
# No more sprites, no random number; without Berserker nothing changes. Not a bug of the prototype: a port feature.
